es, live\nstreams, or asynchronous tasks delivered by webhook.\n\n**Authentication.** Every `/v1` endpoint needs an API key, sent as\n`Authorization: Bearer ytdl_…` or `X-API-Key: ytdl_…`. Keys are issued by\nadministrators and shown only once.\n\n**Roles.** Users can retrieve media, manage their own tasks, and read their\nown account and request history. Everything that changes data (users, API\nkeys, catalog) and everything not owned by the caller needs the `admin`\nrole.\n\n**Choosing the source.** Retrieval endpoints take `url` (a link) or `name`\n(a search query). When both are given, `url` wins.\n\n**Storage.** Retrieved files are stored and never downloaded twice. Files\nnot requested for the configured idle period (default 7 days) are deleted\nand are downloaded again on the next request.\n\n**Idempotency.** `GET /v1/files` is idempotent. For `POST /v1/tasks`, an\n`Idempotency-Key` header makes a repeat return the same task. Without the\nheader, an identical request returns the existing task while it is running\nor its result is still downloadable.\n\n**Rate limits** are per API key; exceeding them returns `429` with\n`Retry-After`. **Read responses** (lists, history, `/v1/me`) may be served\nfrom a short-lived cache, reported in `X-Cache`.\n\n**Errors** always have the body `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`.\n","title":"ytdl-service API","version":"1.0.0"},"openapi":"3.0.3","paths":{"/docs":{"get":{"operationId":"docs","responses":{"200":{"content":{"text/html":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}},"description":"HTML page."}},"security":[],"summary":"Interactive API documentation (Swagger UI)","tags":["Docs"]}},"/healthz":{"get":{"operationId":"healthz","responses":{"200":{"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"status":{"enum":["ok"],"type":"string"}},"required":["status"],"type":"object"}}},"description":"The process is up."}},"security":[],"summary":"Liveness probe","tags":["Health"]}},"/openap